A||||2||Gokart||Fuse block replacement||||5
Z||000000||Gokart||11-21-1999||03:26 PM||||I would like to replace my fuse block in my GT with the one in my parts car. The copper slots that hold the fuses are breaking apart and is what caused my near heart failure last summer when I was told I would need a new engine by the dealer, when it was a worn out TBI slot in the block the whole time! Will it be OK if I dissconnect the negative bat cable then cut all the wires behind the block then splice the new block to the existing wires? TIA!||||reg||5
Z||000001||dogtired||11-22-1999||01:18 PM||||OK lets start this off with I have never done what you are suggesting.<BR>I believe I would look for a donar car and remove the harness, and install it in your car. I have done this on other cars (not fiero) and it takes a lot of paitents and time.<BR>I personally would not cut any (ANY) wire in this harness.<BR>If you cut all the wires and splice / solder / shrink wrap each, you will have a good chance of success, but it will not look very good and will always be a potential for failures in the future. Such a cold solder joints, broken connections, pulled wires and hot spots.<BR>Again I have not done this, but I chringe every time I see a cut and repaired wireing harness in any car. <BR>Just thought I would share my thoughts!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000002||Gokart||11-23-1999||08:32 PM||||Thanks for replying. Maybe I'll try to replace the broken copper slots with the better ones from the block in my parts car instead of cutting wires.||||reg||1
